cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A calibrated indicator battery for AI consciousness, and what survives perturbing it"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this work and the indicator
  framework it implements.

  Cite version 3.0.2 (10.5281/zenodo.23150723), the current version to cite. It
  shares the concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23101902 with every prior version, so
  that concept DOI always resolves to the latest.

  Version history, all metadata-only; no code, result, or claim differs across
  them. 1.0.0 (10.5281/zenodo.23101903) published its references as 722
  one-character array entries instead of four citations. 2.0.0
  (10.5281/zenodo.23111535) corrected that. 3.0.0 (10.5281/zenodo.23122664) was
  the first version whose archive rebuilds byte-for-byte from the repository.
  3.0.1 (10.5281/zenodo.23137224) is superseded and should not be cited: its
  description claimed byte-for-byte rebuildability of an archive that did not
  have it, because the draft was built from a tree with an uncommitted edit.
  3.0.2 exists only to correct that claim. 3.0.1 remains citable but wrong.

  All versions carry zero subjects and no version note, because both fields are
  silently discarded by Zenodo's deposition API; see HANDOFF.md section 2.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A known-answer-gated scoring instrument over the 14 indicator properties
  derived from neuroscientific theories of consciousness by Butlin, Long et al.
  (2023), together with a robustness arm that jointly perturbs every
  discretionary parameter to test how much of the output survives the
  arbitrariness in the aggregation choices. The battery reports a calibrated
  credence with a decomposable interval and never returns a boolean. No AI
  system was scored, and no claim is made about whether any system is conscious.
authors:
  - name: "ScientificDiscoveryLab contributors"
keywords:
